    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a clean, additive derived property:\n\n- **Right unit.** `getMembershipTier()` is computed purely from the `Owner`'s own fields (`namesakeCount`, `email`), so it belongs as a derived getter on the `Owner` entity \u2014 not in a controller, service, or DTO. A maintainer would expect to find it exactly here, next to `getNamesakeCount()`.\n- **No duplication / no catch-all.** It introduces one small cohesive method; `Owner` already carries person/pet accessors, so one more read-only derived accessor doesn't turn it into a grab-bag.\n- **Idiomatic.** The null-guarded boolean checks and ternary are straightforward Java, and the Javadoc mirrors the spec. The OpenAPI addition follows the surrounding schema style precisely (`title`/`description`/`example`/`readOnly: true`, like the adjacent `namesakeCount`), with an `enum` constraining the two documented values.\n\nThe structure is already clean; no changes needed.",
